---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ui } from '../../i18n/ui.ts';
import { withBase } from '../../utils/paths.ts';

const t = ui.en || ui.de;
const philosophyImg = withBase('/uploads/2019/09/galen-crout-0_xMuEbpFAQ-unsplash-1024x684.jpg');
---

<Layout lang='en'>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Philosophy</h1>

        <h2>The Six Characteristics of SHORINJI KEMPO</h2>
        <p>The philosophy of Shorinji Kempo is based on six foundational pillars:</p>

        <ul class="principles-list">
            <li><strong>Ken Zen Ichinyo (Unity of Ken and Zen)</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Riki Ai Funi (Strength and Love in Harmony)</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Shushu Koju (Defense Before Attack)</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Fusatsu Katsujin (Protect People Without Harming)</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Go Ju Ittai (Hard and Soft Together)</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Kumite Shutai (Emphasis on Partnership)</strong></li>
        </ul>

        <h3>1) Ken Zen Ichinyo (Unity of Ken and Zen)</h3>
        <p>Ken means body and Zen means mind. Body and mind are inseparably connected and form a unity that influences each other. In Shorinji Kempo, body and mind are trained in a balanced way, not just one-sided.</p>

        <h3>2) Riki Ai Funi (Strength and Love in Harmony)</h3>
        <p>Even if you are full of compassion and have a great sense of justice, without strength you cannot help anyone. As much strength as you have, without pride and conviction you cannot properly apply it. The harmony of strength and love, as well as reason and compassion, is the guiding principle for our actions.</p>

        <h3>3) Shushu Koju (Defense Before Attack)</h3>
        <p>The combat techniques of Shorinji Kempo are meant to protect oneself from unjust violence. Therefore, it is a system where defense comes first, followed by the counterattack. By taking a secure defensive position, the opponent's attack can be waited out and an effective counterattack executed.</p>

        <h3>4) Fusatsu Katsujin (Protect People Without Harming)</h3>
        <p>The techniques of Shorinji Kempo are developed so that no one gets injured, but rather to protect yourself and others and let them live. We train Shorinji Kempo techniques so that we discover the development potential of people and rejoice in their progress.</p>

        <h3>5) Go Ju Ittai (Hard and Soft Together)</h3>
        <p>Shorinji Kempo techniques consist of "hard techniques" (Goho) like blocking, avoiding, and counterattacking with the body against punches and kicks, as well as "soft techniques" (Juho) like avoiding, throwing, holding, levering, or rotational movements at joints against an attacker who grabs your wrist or clothing. Through skillful combination of hard and soft techniques, their effectiveness can be doubled.</p>

        <h3>6) Kumite Shutai (Emphasis on Partnership)</h3>
        <p>In Shorinji Kempo, training with a partner is the rule. This serves to practice practical techniques so as to be able to respond appropriately and flexibly to the partner's movements. Only through cooperation of both partners can progress be achieved.</p>

        <div class="philosophy-image">
            <img src={philosophyImg} alt="Shorinji Kempo Philosophy" />
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .container {
        max-width: 1100px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 4rem 20px;
    }
    h1, h2, h3 {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        color: #111;
    }
    h2 {
        margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    .principles-list {
        background: #f8f9fa;
        border-left: 4px solid #c00;
        padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
        margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem 0;
        list-style: none;
    }
    .principles-list li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .principles-list li:last-child {
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    h3 {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        padding-top: 2rem;
        border-top: 1px solid #eee;
        color: #c00;
    }
    .philosophy-image {
        margin-top: 3rem;
        text-align: center;
    }
    .philosophy-image img {
        max-width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        border-radius: 8px;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
    }
</style>